// The barkeep's side of the tavern. Open this folder in VS Code with the
// Yarn Spinner extension to edit it; the game compiles it with `loadYarn`.

title: Start
---
<<declare $price = 3>>
<<detour Greeting>>
<<jump Menu>>
===

title: Menu
---
// `$after_song` is set by the Bard node and cleared here, so this line only
// follows the song itself. (`visited("Bard")` would stay true for good.)
<<if $after_song>>
    <<set $after_song to false>>
    Barkeep: Enjoyed the song? #line:menu_after_song
<<else>>
    Barkeep: What'll it be? #line:menu
<<endif>>
-> Order a drink ({$price} coins) <<if $coins >= $price>> #disabled #line:order
    <<detour Drink>>
-> Listen to the bard #line:listen
    <<jump Bard>>
-> Any rumours? <<once>> #line:rumours
    Barkeep: They say the old mill is [wave]haunted[/wave]. #line:rumour_mill
-> Goodnight #line:goodnight
    Barkeep: Safe travels! #line:safe_travels
    <<stop>>
<<jump Menu>>
===

title: Drink
---
<<pay {$price}>>
Barkeep: One Lantern Ale, coming up. #line:ale
<<wait 1>>
<<if visited_count("Drink") >= 1>>
    Barkeep: Another one? You'll float home. [pause=400/] #line:another
<<endif>>
===
